  "body": "Orabona v10 printed p.2/PDF p.14 describes regret as at most sublinear and also displays an ordinary limit inequality. The shared `NoRegret` API expresses eventual upper-epsilon control. This change preserves both meanings and proves their equivalence **only when every fixed feasible comparator's actual normalized regret has a finite real limit**. These limits may depend on the comparator and may be negative.\n\nThe public shared module contains nine derived reconciliation proofs and three definitions. A single fixed affine loss stream on `[0,1]`, with a feasible constant-zero causal learner, telescopes to signed regret. Upper control holds for every feasible comparator. At the fixed feasible comparator **`u=1`**, normalized regret is `-1` on positive even horizons and `0` on odd horizons, so it has no ordinary real limit at that comparator. Its signed coefficients are unbounded over time: this is not a squared-loss or uniformly bounded-loss example and makes no nonconvergence claim about `meanPredict`. Generic supplied-trace bridges are not generic algorithm or minimizer producers. The nine proofs are derived support, not nine printed book theorems.\n\nExisting comparator regret, upper semantics and the actual strict-past mean predictor are reused. The old `OnlineLearningAsymptotic` mathematical code is byte-preserved; a separately reviewed trailing source-qualified comment distinguishes the ordinary-limit display from the existing mean upper producer. One source card, six public notes and twelve new nodes use the same underlying Lean declaration registry and Book graph. All 10,894 prior node IDs, URLs and statement hashes remain unchanged.\n\nValidation evidence is in `runs/online-no-regret-20261008/` and `docs/contracts/online-no-regret-v1/`:\n\n- Actual focused builds, 15 named nondegenerate canary proofs, and `#print axioms` for 34 scoped declarations: only standard Lean axioms, no `sorryAx`.\n- Actual equality compilation for 12 neutral terminal/reused propositions, 15 canary types and 7 whole definitions; 24 native header guards and 19 compiled proof-value dependency pairs. Native safe verification alone is not Lean compilation.\n- Combined public root and `Tests` builds after the reviewed source-comment append (9,095 and 9,249 jobs); full `python tools/bandit.py check` (472 tests, 7 skipped); scoped frontier shadow.\n- Nonvacuous committed exact-base contributor gate: six production paths and one changed manifest. The earlier zero-path N/A result and subsequent rejected unchanged-file manifest are retained with their repairs.\n- Applicable clean local site from `41a225167ca778e891fb6af8d0a61ed3083878e9`, site/registry checks, current browser DOM and 12 individually viewed images. No local build is presented as deployment.\n- Distinct staged source CONTRACT, BODY and FINAL reviewer accepted with explicit delta; the distinct blind decoder reconstructed the neutral statements only. Original R1–R8 reader requirements are individually discharged. These are disclosed automated roles, not human/external review or a single runtime-enforced workflow.\n\nThis draft PR is stacked on **open, unmerged PR #191**, exact head `1737391d9867a420a9e4b9529d4d90e1bf79c93c`, with base `codex/research-online-log-lower`. Only the **C1-NOREGRET source subobligation** closes. Chapter 1 still requires full regret/best-minimum mapping and five other main-relative source-module audits; that diagnostic remains failed and unwaived. The original 16 Chapter 1 source items have an unknown required proof total. Chapter 2 remains incomplete; Chapters 3–16 and necessary appendix dependencies remain required. The whole-book Goal remains active. No merge, main update, deployment or worktree retirement is included.\n",
